From dbb84826f556bb64ade46b9c0d755a0971f23a56 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 11:50:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/11] i686 peephole: fuse accumulator immediates into slot
 stores (Pattern 2b-mem)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

'movl $X, %eax; mov{l,w,b} %eax/%ax/%al, SLOT' becomes a direct
immediate store when %eax is dead afterwards: movw saves 3 bytes,
movb 4, movl 1, and the accumulator round-trip disappears. W/B forms
truncate a numeric immediate to the store width; the L form may carry
a symbol. Two guards keep it profitable and sound:
 * a re-read of the same slot inside the deadness window blocks the
   fusion (forward_slot_loads would have deleted that reload for free
   in the unfused shape — fusing would trade a 4-byte reload for a
   1-3 byte saving);
 * zero idioms (xorl/subl %eax,%eax) count as kills, not reads.

x86-64 already emits direct immediate stores from codegen (verified);
nothing to port. Realmode boot corpus: 33875 -> 33525 bytes.
840/840 unit, 50/50 correctness, 9/9 checks, regparm all levels,
nbody -O0 exact, uchar matrix.
