From 6840bd09c98fd46a7b989354d4893a95ea571492 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 13:01:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/11] i686: call indirect through global function pointers
 without a stack stage
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Under regparm every i686 argument register (%eax/%ecx/%edx) is taken at
an indirect call, so the emitter stages the target through a stack slot:
'movl SYM,%eax; movl %eax,N(%esp); ... call *N(%esp)' — 11 bytes of
load+spill per site that GCC never emits (it calls '*pio_ops' directly).
The setup corpus has 74 such sites (pio_ops/vga_modes dispatch).

New peephole fold_global_fnptr_calls (phase 3.7): per function, collect
load/spill/call triples whose crossed lines are register/immediate-only
data ops that never READ the staged register (pure overwrites are fine —
that is exactly the regparm arg staging); then, per displacement, fold
ALL triples iff every textual reference to that N(%esp) belongs to a
triple. The whole-slot ownership rule makes the fold immune to ESP
renumbering arguments: no other reader of any of those physical slots
exists under any numbering. Volatile pointers stay a single read, only
moved across non-memory ops, which volatile semantics do not constrain.

The internal assemblers could not encode the result: 'call *sym' /
'jmp *sym' (FF /2, FF /4 with disp-only ModR/M) added to i686
(byte-exact vs GAS: ff 15/ff 25 + R_386_32 in .code32, ff 16/ff 26 +
R_386_16 in .code16 — same 16-bit pointer read gcc -m16 emits) and the
matching Label arm was already unreachable on x86-64 paths lccc emits;
i686 only. Runtime matrix: fnptr dispatch through struct + volatile fp +
store-between-load-and-call at -O0..-Os x regparm on/off, all pass.

Realmode boot corpus: 33354 -> 33194 bytes (16 folds; remaining 61
sites are mixed-use slots the ownership rule correctly refuses).
3 new unit tests; 841+3 unit, 50/50 correctness, 9/9 checks, regparm
conformance all levels, nbody -O0 exact.
