MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The slot-ownership proof folds a displacement only when EVERY reference
in the function belongs to a candidate triple — one interleaved use of
the slot for something else blocked all 39 remaining pio_ops dispatch
sites (slot 0 is the emitter's favorite scratch).

Second, per-triple proof (linear seal): walking forward from the call
across straight-line code only (no label, no branch/ret, no push/pop,
no ESP arithmetic), the FIRST access overlapping the slot's 4 bytes is
an exact full-width movl store. Then the staged value is observable
only by our call, and folding is sound regardless of what the rest of
the function does with the slot. Chains of same-slot triples fold by
induction: each member's own window+walk is branch-free, so removing
earlier pairs never exposes a reader. Overlap windows ([d-3,d+3] for
the textual scan) block partial-width aliasing in both proofs.

Realmode boot corpus: 33138 -> 32926 bytes (32 more sites folded).
2 new unit tests: the reuse-chain fold and the branch-before-reseal
block. 850/850 unit, 50/50 correctness, 9/9 checks, regparm all
levels, fnptr runtime matrix, nbody -O0 exact.
